# TypeScript Standards

## Type Safety

- Never use `any` type unless absolutely necessary with documented justification
- Fix type errors immediately rather than working around them
- Use `supabase gen types` for database types
- Prefer strict TypeScript configuration

## Naming Conventions

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Descriptive naming
const isUserAuthenticated = checkAuth();
const handleFormSubmit = () => {};
const UserProfileCard: React.FC = () => {};

// ❌ BAD - Vague naming
const x = checkAuth();
const fn = () => {};
const Comp: React.FC = () => {};
```

## Unused Variables

Use underscore prefix for intentionally unused parameters:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const handleEvent = (_event: Event) => {
  // We don't need the event, just that it happened
};

// ❌ BAD - Will trigger linter warning
const handleEvent = (event: Event) => {};
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Swallowing errors
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD - Proper error handling
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Failed to fetch data:', error);
  throw error;
}
```
